SUMMARY:7th European Meeting on AMPK & Nutrient-Sensing Pathways 2026
LOCATION:Lunteren\, Netherlands
DESCRIPTION:Triennial European meeting on AMPK and nutrient-sensing signall
 ing. Published program includes dedicated sessions 'Beyond AMPK: nutrient-
 sensing pathways in health and diseases'\, 'AMPK family in cancer\, aging 
 and longevity'\, and 'AMPK and nutrient sensors in organelle biology'.\n\n
 Why it matters for mTOR (★★): AMPK is the principal upstream antagonis
 t of mTORC1: it inhibits mTORC1 both directly (Raptor Ser792) and via TSC2
 \, the exact wiring already in the Atlas corpus (Shaw / Inoki / Gwinn). Th
 e program's explicit 'Beyond AMPK: nutrient-sensing pathways' and 'AMPK fa
 mily in cancer\, aging and longevity' sessions cover mTOR as the reciproca
 l arm of energy sensing. UPDATE (2026-07-22): official speaker list is now
  published and does NOT include Hardie or Shaw as previously speculated\; 
 confirmed speakers instead include Atlas authors Hongbo Chi (immunometabol
 ism/AMPK-mTOR crosstalk in T cells) and Thomas Weichhart (mTOR/immunometab
 olism)\, both re-linked below in place of Shaw RJ.\n\nSpeakers or organise
 rs with a profile in the Atlas: Hongbo Chi\, Thomas Weichhart\n\nConferenc
 e site: https://www.atoutcom.com/ampk/\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://
 mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-7th-european-meeting-on-ampk-nutrient-sensing-pa
 thways-2026
